Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 03:01:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 190/307] feat: LPV specular GI (r_LPVSpecular) - v2 item 1

Short voxel march along the reflected eye vector in the apply pass,
the same approximation CryEngine 3 shipped: 3 cells, inverse square
step weighting, radiance evaluated towards the surface via the SH
direction basis. Output goes to a second screen target ($LPVSpecular)
through the fade / intensity / MaxIrradiance chain, and plugs into the
engine specular GI sockets: TiledShading slot 11 for deferred (ApplyGI
mode 3 adds spec x surface reflectance) and forward slot 47 (same mode
3 branch, automatic). r_LPVSpecular 0 binds the black texture and skips
the march entirely.

The L1 SH grid is too coarse for mirror images - this gives metals and
wet surfaces a broad directional indirect reflection, sharp reflections
remain SSR/probe territory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
